            <ArticleTitle>Nutritional interventions to reduce symptoms in children and adults with attention deficit hyperactivity disorder: a scoping review protocol.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>2265-2269</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.11124/JBISRIR-2016-003134</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="REVIEW QUESTION/OBJECTIVE:" NlmCategory="UNASSIGNED">The objective of this scoping review is to examine and map reported nutritional interventions and their outcomes in relieving symptoms of attention deficit hyperactivity disorder (ADHD) in the daily lives of children and adults. A further objective is to determine if experiences of people diagnosed with ADHD, their relatives or staff in being on a diet or having to eat or avoid eating specific food items have been reported in the existing literature.Specifically the scoping review questions are.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
